        "title": "Unique, interesting and very cultural",
        "text": "I thought I may be uncomfortable visiting, given that people are cremated at pashpupatinath and I didn't want to encroach on people saying goodbye to their loved ones. However, this was not the case - it is culturally very different and it was actually a very peaceful place of worship, reflection and community. I would recommend going at sunset to catch the music and lamps, and to hire a guide to clue you into everything that is going on. One of my favourite places I visited during my stay.",
