      {
        "review_id": 484528525,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r484528525-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Abode of Shiva",
        "text": "A significant temple to visit for Hindus, the sprawling temple complex is also a UNESCO World Heritage Site. A visit is accompanied with the usual crowds but leaves one in thrall too of the amazing number of shiv lingas installed there. Apparently the complex has over 100,000 shiv lingas. The complex is dominated at the entrance by a giant statue of Nandi. A spiritually satisfying visit. In spite of the thronging crowds, the process of darshan is hassle free and without the expected discomfort. A must visit if you are in Nepal.",
