        "review_id": 484463611,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r484463611-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Is a famous, sacred Hindu temple",
        "text": "My friend and I visited this temple on April 4,2017 as part of our tour in Nepal. It is considered the oldest Hindu temple of Kathmandu. Countless smaller temples were constructed around the main temple on both banks of Bagmati River during the last few centuries. it is a UNESCO Cultural Heritage Site \nThere are numerous legends, connected with the construction of the temple. The most famous one claims, that the temple was built on the site where Shiva lost one of his antlers, while he was in the guise of a deer. He and his wife arrived to the bank of Bagmati and amazed by the beauty of the site decided to change themselves into deers and walk in the surrounding forests.\nIt was an excellent experience. A great place to learn about Hindu customs and funeral rituals. The main temple is restricted to Hindus only but the rest of the sprawling complex is open to anyone.\nThe upper river banks are for high caste cremations, and the lower banks are for low castes. \nFor foreigner the entrance fee is 1000 Rs approximately 8€ or $ 11. It worth the visit.",
