      {
        "review_id": 484458803,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r484458803-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Religious and leisure ",
        "text": "This place is out of this world and there is a reason why the main temple is for hindu's only. I visited on the day of Budhdha Poornima and there was a special tantric Puja held with around 86 dishes made for the lord Pashupatinath. I felt so overwhelmed and sacred just to be present at that moment . Hinduism is an old religion with many layers and requires deep knowledge and will to understand. I was fortunate to see the sacrifice as well. This was the most authentic temples I have visited. Faint hearted should stay at their hotels and enjoy as this is not a park it is a place of great religious significance. please don't expect it to be pretty as this a place of lord Shiva who is the god for all and every living beings and being who lived once. Om Namah Shivay!!!!",
