      {
        "review_id": 483366470,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r483366470-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Get a guide and the price drops....",
        "text": "Pashupatinath Temple where a celebration was going on so it was very busy, but in a good way. Lots of locals in celebratory mood! A guide took us round to the back of the temple (only Hindus are allowed in the temple itself) to the sacred river, next to which there were open air cremations going on. In Nepalese culture, they bring their dead to the closest temple within a few hours for cremation, usually with fire, followed by many days of celebration. We saw families bringing their loved ones to the river to wash their feet, covered in red, yellow and orange (to signify fire) before being placed on the funeral pyre.",
        "review_tip": null,
